# XCU unget
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.unget.001
anchor     utilities/unget.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/unget.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/unget.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       unget prints the SID that would have been made, removes the
           p-file and g-file, and allows a new get -e.
test       t/001-undo-edit.sh

assertion  XCU.unget.002
anchor     utilities/unget.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -s suppresses the SID line and -n keeps the g-file.
test       t/002-options-s-n.sh

assertion  XCU.unget.003
anchor     utilities/unget.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/unget.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       unget with no pending edit gives a non-zero status, and a -
           operand reads names from standard input.
test       t/003-errors.sh

assertion  XCU.unget.004
anchor     utilities/unget.html#OPTIONS/-r
class      required
since      1992
says       With two outstanding edits by the same user, -r names the one to
           cancel and the other remains pending.
test       t/004-r-two-edits.sh

assertion  XCU.unget.005
anchor     utilities/unget.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       With several files, or a directory, each pathname is written on a
           line of its own after a blank line, followed by the SID removed.
test       t/005-multiple-files.sh
